## Why This Is Asked
Tests for data export reflect real user needs and often fail on data mismatch or flaky downloads. This question probes data seeding, UI actions, file verification, and cross-browser handling.

## Key Concepts
- Data seeding and isolation
- End-to-end file download verification
- Network/mocked API endpoints
- Cross-browser testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example snippet
test('export selected rows', async ({ page, browserName }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  await seedData(20);
  await page.click('#filter');
  await page.check('input[name="select-row-1"]');
  await page.check('input[name="select-row-2"]');
  const [ download ] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('#export-csv')
  ]);
  const path = await download.path();
  // read and verify CSV content deterministically
  const csv = await require('fs').promises.readFile(path, 'utf8');
  // parse and validate headers + 2 selected rows by IDs
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle large datasets (>1000 rows) for export?
- How would you ensure exported CSV ordering remains deterministic across runs?

## Why This Is Asked
Probes ability to design robust E2E tests for streaming pipelines, focusing on exactly-once semantics, replay safety, fault injection, and cross-store validation.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end streaming tests across Kafka, storage, and materialized views
- Exactly-once and idempotent writes
- Replay/failure scenarios and broker partition events
- Tenant data isolation and deterministic mocks
- Observability: SLA validation and latency metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo end-to-end test flow for streaming ingestion
async function testStreamingPipeline() {
  const tenantId = uniqueTenant();
  seedTenant(tenantId);
  produceKafkaEvents(tenantId, 10000);
  waitForSink(tenantId);
  replaySubset(tenantId, 1000);
  verifyNoDuplicates(tenantId);
  simulateBrokerFailure();
  validateEventualConsistency(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate idempotency across multiple partitions?
- Which metrics and alarms would you configure for failure scenarios?

